ANIMATION PROMPT — EGO HYGIENE COVER
EDITION 1: ORIENTATION

Create a subtle looping animation of the existing magazine cover.

This is not a cinematic scene.
This is a living printed artifact.

The frame must remain completely locked.
No zoom.
No push-in.
No pan.
No rotation.
No perspective change.
No parallax.
The page does not move.

The animation should feel like a still image that is gently alive — similar to moving portraits in an old magical world.

PRESERVE:
- Exact composition
- Typography placement
- Paper texture
- Grain and wear
- Layout integrity

ALLOWED MOTION (very subtle only):

1. Crystal Glow
- Soft prismatic shimmer within the crystal facets
- Light shifts across surfaces slowly
- No sparkle bursts
- No lens flares

2. Ambient Atmosphere
- Faint drifting dust particles
- Subtle floating specks in background
- Must feel like aged air, not digital effects

3. Background Energy
- Extremely slight mist movement behind silhouette
- Slow breathing luminosity in the dark teal sky
- No character movement

4. Light Pass
- A gentle warm light shift across the page surface
- Like candlelight flicker
- Does not change color dramatically

FORBIDDEN:
- Text movement
- Title flicker
- Badge movement
- Silhouette animation
- Camera movement
- Frame shift
- Modern visual effects
- Excessive glow

LOOP:
- 8–12 seconds
- Seamless loop
- End in identical visual state to beginning
- No fade out

TONE:
- Subtle
- Mystical
- Printed artifact
- Calm and alive

GOAL:
Make the magazine cover feel gently illuminated and breathing while remaining completely still as a printed object.
